# Phase-1.1 acceptance: select -> gather -> build -> produce -> HUD -> menu.
# Frames are 1-based. Coordinates are screen pixels at the starting camera.
#
# Two rules this script exists to enforce:
#   * every build and produce command goes through the command card, never a
#     hotkey — the point is to prove the shipped *pointer* path, and a hotkey
#     bypasses the grid's own selection/enable/hit-test logic;
#   * every worker the card acts on is really selected first. `find_builder`
#     falls back to "any live worker", so a placement can succeed with an
#     empty selection — the card cannot, and neither may this run.
#
# The selection clicks therefore all land in the first ~40 frames, while the
# six relocated workers (T3) are still near the spawn cells named below. T13
# lets an active gather pair pass through its partner instead of shouldering
# it aside, so the group leaves those cells sooner than it used to: the two
# builder clicks are timed for the faster departure, not the old one.
#
# T7 re-authored every world coordinate below. The HQ is now 24 cells, so the
# camera opens on its centre (172,172) and the screen formula is
# sx = 960 + 4*(x - y), sy = 540 + 2*(x + y - 344); the spawn row moved out of
# the enlarged footprint to y = 190. The Depot plot moved east and the
# Barracks plot west because both old plots are now inside the HQ, and every
# min corner is floored onto the 8-cell build square.

1:move:960,540
5:drag:800,520,940,620         # box-select the six starting workers (T3 scatters them wider than one row)
10:rclick:897,387              # crystal node, one pixel inside its visible quad [896,386,48,48] (ground 920,434)
12:lclick:872,567              # narrow to one already-selected worker (its ground point at frame 12) — a re-select is silent
16:rclick:1049,535             # gas node, one pixel inside its visible quad [1048,534,48,48] (ground 1072,582)
20:rclick:1900,100             # off the map, one worker selected: exactly one Reject

# --- Depot, built by one boxed worker --------------------------------------
#
# A *box* around a single worker, not a click on it: at this frame the six
# bodies are still close enough that their pick shapes overlap, and only the
# box reads ground points alone. The box holds exactly one of them.
22:drag:780,520,830,552        # the Depot builder, alone in its box
24:lclick:1800,888             # command slot 1 = Depot ghost
26:move:928,622
27:lclick:928,622              # cursor cell (188,196) -> min corner (184,192), south-east of the HQ
28:rclick:928,622              # order that worker onto its own site: one Build receipt

# --- Barracks, built by a second boxed worker -------------------------------
40:drag:834,500,880,524        # the Barracks builder, alone in its box
42:lclick:1872,888             # command slot 2 = Barracks ghost
44:move:896,494
45:lclick:896,494              # cursor cell (152,168) -> min corner (144,160), west of the HQ
46:rclick:896,494              # order that worker onto its own site: one Build receipt

# --- a Worker from the HQ ---
120:lclick:960,494             # select the HQ, at its own footprint corner (160.5,160.5)
125:lclick:1728,888            # command slot 0 = Worker

# --- a Soldier from the Barracks ---
900:lclick:896,494              # select the finished Barracks (footprint centre 152,168)
905:lclick:1728,888            # command slot 0 = Soldier

# --- the minimap, then the nested menu ---
1310:lclick:360,960            # minimap, inside the diamond's right half (map ~298,22)
1320:lclick:1888,24            # MENU_RECT centre -> paused menu
1330:lclick:960,540            # SETTINGS -> settings panel
1340:lclick:1170,288           # keyboard-pan slider -> 78 cells/s
1350:key:esc                   # settings -> menu
1360:key:esc                   # menu -> gameplay; the sim resumes

# --- look away from the base ---
1400:pan:right                 # hold the right arrow
1500:panup:right               # release it

1520:key:f1                    # overlay on for the final frames
1560:quit
